{"id":"mahabharata-7-033","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":33,"title":"त्रयस्त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 33 · The Pandava and Kaurava lines","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya describes the Pandava heroes, red-clad and red-bannered, advancing with Dhrishtadyumna, and the Kaurava leaders posted in the wheel formation. Jayadratha is placed at its rear with Shakuni, Shalya and Bhurishravas around him.","kn":"ಕೆಂಪು ವಸ್ತ್ರ, ಧ್ವಜಗಳ ಪಾಂಡವ ವೀರರು ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುನ್ನಡೆಯುವುದನ್ನೂ ಚಕ್ರವ್ಯೂಹದಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಂತ ಕೌರವ ನಾಯಕರನ್ನೂ ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜಯದ್ರಥನನ್ನು ಹಿಂಭಾಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಶಕುನಿ, ಶಲ್ಯ, ಭೂರಿಶ್ರವರೊಡನೆ ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ.","hi":"संजय लाल वस्त्र और ध्वजा वाले पाण्डव वीरों का धृष्टद्युम्न के साथ आगे बढ़ना और चक्रव्यूह में खड़े कौरव नायकों का वर्णन करते हैं। जयद्रथ को पीछे शकुनि, शल्य और भूरिश्रवा के साथ रखा गया है।","te":"ఎరుపు వస్త్రాలు, ధ్వజాల పాండవ వీరులు ధృష్టద్యుమ్నునితో ముందుకు సాగడాన్ని, చక్రవ్యూహంలో నిలిచిన కౌరవ నాయకులను సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. జయద్రథుని వెనుక శకుని, శల్య, భూరిశ్రవులతో ఉంచారు.","ta":"சிவப்பு ஆடை, கொடிகளுடன் த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனோடு முன்னேறும் பாண்டவ வீரரையும் சக்கர வியூகத்தில் நிற்கும் கௌரவத் தலைவரையும் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான். ஜயத்ரதன் பின்புறம் சகுனி, சல்யன், பூரிசிரவஸ் சூழ நிறுத்தப்பட்டுள்ளான்.","ml":"ചുവന്ന വസ്ത്രവും ചുവന്ന കൊടിയുമുള്ള പാണ്ഡവ വീരന്മാർ ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനോടൊപ്പം മുന്നേറുന്നതും കൗരവ നേതാക്കൾ ചക്രാകൃതിയിൽ നിൽക്കുന്നതും സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ജയദ്രഥനെ അതിന്റെ പിന്നിൽ ശകുനി, ശല്യർ, ഭൂരിശ്രവസ്സ് എന്നിവർ വലയം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.33; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अभिमन्युवधपर्व","titleEn":"Abhimanyuvadha Parva (Slaying of Abhimanyu)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"समरेऽत्युग्रकर्माणः कर्मभिर्व्यञ्जितश्रमाः ।\nसकृष्णाः पाण्डवाः पञ्च देवैरपि दुरासदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Pandavas, fierce in action in battle, whose labors are shown by their deeds, with Krishna, were hard to approach even for gods."}},{"n":2,"text":"सत्त्वकर्मान्वयैर्बुद्ध्या प्रकृत्या यशसा श्रिया ।\nनैव भूतो न भविता कृष्णतुल्यगुणः पुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In strength, deeds, lineage, intelligence, nature, fame and splendor, no man has been or will be equal in virtues to Krishna."}},{"n":3,"text":"सत्यधर्मपरो दाता विप्रपूजादिभिर्गुणैः ।\nसदैव त्रिदिवं प्राप्तो राजा किल युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira, devoted to truth and dharma, a giver, and having virtues such as honoring Brahmins, is said always to have reached heaven."}},{"n":4,"text":"युगान्ते चान्तको राजञ्जामदग्न्यश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nरणस्थो भीमसेनश्च कथ्यन्ते सदृशास्त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of an age, Death, the mighty Jamadagni's son Rama, and Bhimasena in battle are said to be three alike."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रतिज्ञाकर्मदक्षस्य रणे गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nउपमां नाधिगच्छामि पार्थस्य सदृशीं क्षितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I find no comparison on earth for Partha, bearer of Gandiva, skilled in keeping his pledges and deeds in battle."}},{"n":6,"text":"गुरुवात्सल्यमत्यन्तं नैभृत्यं विनयो दमः ।\nनकुलेऽप्रातिरूप्यं च शौर्यं च नियतानि षट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great affection for elders, modesty, humility, self-control, and unmatched heroism and beauty are the six fixed qualities in Nakula."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रुतगाम्भीर्यमाधुर्यसत्त्ववीर्यपराक्रमैः ।\nसदृशो देवयोर्वीरः सहदेवः किलाश्विनोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In learning, depth, sweetness, strength, courage and valor, the hero Sahadeva is said to be like the two Ashvins."}},{"n":8,"text":"ये च कृष्णे गुणाः स्फीताः पाण्डवेषु च ये गुणाः ।\nअभिमन्यौ किलैकस्था दृश्यन्ते गुणसंचयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever abundant virtues are in Krishna and in the Pandavas are all seen gathered in Abhimanyu alone."}},{"n":9,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य धैर्येण कृष्णस्य चरितेन च ।\nकर्मभिर्भीमसेनस्य सदृशो भीमकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In steadiness he was like Yudhishthira, in conduct like Krishna, in deeds like Bhimasena of terrible deeds,"}},{"n":10,"text":"धनंजयस्य रूपेण विक्रमेण श्रुतेन च ।\nविनयात्सहदेवस्य सदृशो नकुलस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"in beauty, valor and learning like Dhananjaya, and in humility like Sahadeva and Nakula."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"अभिमन्युमहं सूत सौभद्रमपराजितम् ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छामि कार्त्स्न्येन कथमायोधने हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, I wish to hear in full how Subhadra's son Abhimanyu, the unconquered, was killed in battle."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"चक्रव्यूहो महाराज आचार्येणाभिकल्पितः ।\nतत्र शक्रोपमाः सर्वे राजानो विनिवेशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wheel array was devised by the teacher, great king; in it all the kings, like Indra, were placed."}},{"n":13,"text":"संघातो राजपुत्राणां सर्वेषामभवत्तदा ।\nकृताभिसमयाः सर्वे सुवर्णविकृतध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then there was a gathering of all the princes, with agreements made and gold-adorned banners."}},{"n":14,"text":"रक्ताम्बरधराः सर्वे सर्वे रक्तविभूषणाः ।\nसर्वे रक्तपताकाश्च सर्वे वै हेममालिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They all wore red garments and red ornaments, all had red pennants, and all wore gold garlands."}},{"n":15,"text":"तेषां दशसहस्राणि बभूवुर्दृढधन्विनाम् ।\nपौत्रं तव पुरस्कृत्य लक्ष्मणं प्रियदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten thousand of them were firm archers, with your grandson, the fair-looking Lakshmana, in front."}},{"n":16,"text":"अन्योन्यसमदुःखास्ते अन्योन्यसमसाहसाः ।\nअन्योन्यं स्पर्धमानाश्च अन्योन्यस्य हिते रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They shared one another's sorrows and daring, competed with one another, and delighted in one another's good."}},{"n":17,"text":"कर्णदुःशासनकृपैर्वृतो राजा महारथैः ।\nदेवराजोपमः श्रीमाञ्श्वेतच्छत्राभिसंवृतः ।\nचामरव्यजनाक्षेपैरुदयन्निव भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, surrounded by Karna, Duhshasana and Kripa, great chariot-warriors, shining like Indra, king of gods, under a white umbrella, like the rising sun with the waving of fans and yak-tails,"}},{"n":18,"text":"प्रमुखे तस्य सैन्यस्य द्रोणोऽवस्थितनायके ।\nसिन्धुराजस्तथातिष्ठच्छ्रीमान्मेरुरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"stood at the front of that army, with Drona as its leader in position, and the Sindhu king, splendid like Mount Meru, stood there."}},{"n":19,"text":"सिन्धुराजस्य पार्श्वस्था अश्वत्थामपुरोगमाः ।\nसुतास्तव महाराज त्रिंशत्त्रिदशसंनिभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the side of the Sindhu king stood your thirty sons, equal to gods, with Ashvatthaman at their head, O great king."}},{"n":20,"text":"गान्धारराजः कितवः शल्यो भूरिश्रवास्तथा ।\nपार्श्वतः सिन्धुराजस्य व्यराजन्त महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Gandhara, Shalya, and Bhurishravas, the gambler, those great chariot-warriors, shone at the Sindhu king's side."}}]}]}